Marquee's FFmpeg audio decoding: what is in this directory and where it comes from.

FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org), LGPL 2.1 or later.
  No FFmpeg source is kept here. build.sh downloads the release named in versions.properties, checks its SHA-256,
  and builds the audio decoders it lists, without --enable-gpl, --enable-version3 or --enable-nonfree, as the shared
  libraries libavcodec.so, libavutil.so and libswresample.so. Replacing them with libraries rebuilt from the same
  source changes the decoders without touching the rest of the app. The licence text, from that release, is
  src/main/assets/licences/FFmpeg-LGPL-2.1.txt; the app shows it under Settings > Licences.

Media3's FFmpeg extension, Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE.Apache-2.0.txt).
  Copied unmodified from https://github.com/androidx/media at tag 1.11.1 (commit 8c6678b657ed), directory
  libraries/decoder_ffmpeg: src/main/java/androidx/media3/decoder/ffmpeg without ExperimentalFfmpegVideoRenderer.java
  (it decodes no video), and src/main/jni/ffmpeg_jni.cc. build.sh replaces Media3's build_ffmpeg.sh and
  CMakeLists.txt. To move to another Media3 release, copy the same files from its tag and set MEDIA3_VERSION in
  versions.properties.
